{"evidence":["Reviewed /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs, /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/src/lib.rs, and /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs.","`cargo test --test e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes -- --nocapture` passed, but Probe 1 reported `initial=10, final=10, cycles=6/6, juv=7, sub=1`.","`TANK_E2E_VERBOSE=1 cargo test --test e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes all_shrimp_probes_summary -- --nocapture` printed only the summary report; no verbose trace block was emitted.","The summary runner at /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:1289 calls `run_probe_*` helpers, and those helpers build plain `Engine`s at :197, :491, :696, :981, and :1222 without `enable_instrumentation()` or tracer setup.","The chloride probe runs on plain engines at /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:769-812 and then records failures on a new dummy `HarnessRun` built from `TankState::new(SimSeed(0))` at :821-824, with no instrumentation before `finish()`.","The `shrimp_diag` comment says it dumps reserve at /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:56-59, but the formatted output at :61-80 contains no reserve field."],"findings_or_gaps":["High: The success scenario does not validate the required 'population grows' outcome. Its story says growth is expected at /home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:95-97, but the only population assertion is `final >= initial` at :150-159, and the passing run still ends at `initial=10, final=10`.","High: `all_shrimp_probes_summary` is not an instrumented e2e runner, so it does not satisfy the structured-trace acceptance criterion. It executes the `run_probe_*` helpers on raw `Engine`s without tracing, and even with `TANK_E2E_VERBOSE=1` it emits no trace output.","High: The chloride-protection scenario has broken failure diagnostics. Because the real treated/control simulations never use `HarnessRun` or tracing, a failure would produce artifacts from a dummy empty state instead of the actual scenario, with no per-tick trace and no treated/control checkpoints.","Medium: Failure diagnostics are still incomplete versus the contract. `shrimp_diag()` claims to include reserve but does not print any reserve values, and the trace schema only exposes aggregate `animal.reserve_g`, not per-stage reserve state."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Make the breeding probe require net growth under the healthy-tank fixture, or retune the fixture until the long-horizon success scenario actually grows while remaining chemically stable.","Convert the summary runner to execute the real instrumented probe paths, or otherwise attach tracing/artifact capture, so a single `all_shrimp_probes_summary` invocation both prints the report and logs structured traces.","Rewrite the chloride probe around real `HarnessRun` instances for the actual pre-treatment and post-treatment branches, with instrumentation and checkpoints attached to the simulated states rather than a placeholder `TankState::new(...)` run.","Add reserve to failure output, and if the acceptance criterion is meant literally, surface per-stage reserve values in either snapshot diagnostics or recorded trace/checkpoint artifacts."],"outcome":"request_changes"}